<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>$(MeToolkitMauiTargetFrameworks)</TargetFrameworks>
    <UseMaui>true</UseMaui>
    <SingleProject>true</SingleProject>
    <AssemblyName>Me.Toolkit.Maui.Sizing</AssemblyName>
    <RootNamespace>Me.Toolkit.Maui.Sizing</RootNamespace>
    <PackageId>Me.Toolkit.Maui.Sizing</PackageId>
    <Product>Me.Toolkit.Maui.Sizing</Product>
    <Description>Relative sizes for .NET MAUI: a percentage of the parent, the window, the display or another element, in XAML or code.
WidthRequest="{me:Relative 30}" is 30% of the parent's width, and stays that way as the window is resized or the phone rotated. Works on any double property - WidthRequest, HeightRequest, FontSize, Spacing - with Min and Max to clamp it.</Description>
    <PackageTags>maui xaml markup-extension responsive relative size percentage viewport</PackageTags>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>26.9.27 stamps the net10.0 assembly with the package version. 26.9.26 shipped it as 1.0.0.0 - the publish workflow's test step rebuilt that slice without the version before packing - while the Android, iOS, Mac Catalyst and Windows assemblies were right. 26.9.26 is unlisted. Nothing else changed.
First release, 26.9.26.
{me:Relative} and SetRelativeSize size a double property as a percentage of the parent (less its padding), the window, the main display, an element named with x:Reference, or the nearest ancestor of a type. Width, Height, Shorter and Longer pick the dimension; Min and Max clamp the result; Portrait and Landscape give a different percentage for each orientation of the window. To=Self keeps an aspect ratio, Offset gives calc(50% - 8), and RelativeSizing's attached properties let a Style carry a relative size. The value is recomputed whenever the reference changes size or the element moves in the tree.</PackageReleaseNotes>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <!--
      Microsoft.Maui.Controls, unlike the other libraries' Microsoft.Maui.Core: markup extensions,
      bindings, VisualElement and Window all live in Controls, and there is no sizing a XAML element
      without them. Same version as the demo app, and the same line as Core elsewhere.
    -->
    <PackageReference Include="Microsoft.Maui.Controls" Version="10.0.101" />
  </ItemGroup>

  <ItemGroup>
    <InternalsVisibleTo Include="Me.Toolkit.Maui.Tests" />
  </ItemGroup>

</Project>
